            <ArticleTitle>Left main reconstruction as an alternative method to CABG after primary PCI complication.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>259-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ihj.2015.03.018</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0019-4832(15)00085-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Left main coronary artery disease is rare, accounting for 1% of all coronary artery disease and traditionally, is treated by coronary artery bypass grafting. We report our experience and five years follow up, after a coronary osteal surgical plasty in a young man who referred to our center with an anterior myocardial infarction.</AbstractText>
